      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f30ecee654cd4491456a82f|full_name} Thanks for the suggestion! We can certainly experiment with this.\n\nThe objective would be removing the need to refer to a specific instance of a source on a constraint in the animation clip. Once this is possible, it would no longer be necessary to automatically correct the IDs in the animation clip since the bindings would be constant anyway. (Clips can still be automatically updated by the conversion tool triggered by the user, which it needs to do in order to fully convert an object from Unity constraints to VRChat constraints.)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
